  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set required for the listener-container threading refactor across the three repos, ordered by centrality to the change:\n\n**spring-kafka** (primary implementation surface):\n- `ConcurrentMessageListenerContainer.java` / `KafkaMessageListenerContainer.java` \u2014 the single-threaded\u2192concurrent container pair at the heart of the refactor\n- `AbstractMessageListenerContainer.java`, `MessageListenerContainer.java`, `GenericMessageListenerContainer.java` \u2014 the container abstraction hierarchy (lifecycle, `SmartLifecycle` wiring)\n- `ContainerProperties.java` \u2014 carries `listenerTaskExecutor`, ack-mode, and other threading-relevant config\n- `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory.java`, `AbstractKafkaListenerContainerFactory.java`, `KafkaListenerContainerFactory.java` \u2014 factory chain that instantiates containers and applies `concurrency`\n- `EnableKafka.java`, `KafkaListener.java`, `KafkaListenerAnnotationBeanPostProcessor.java` \u2014 annotation-driven endpoint registration that resolves per-listener concurrency\n\n**spring-boot** (autoconfiguration/exposed properties):\n- `KafkaAnnotationDrivenConfiguration.java` \u2014 builds the `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory` bean\n- `KafkaProperties.java` \u2014 exposes `spring.kafka.listener.concurrency`\n- `KafkaAutoConfiguration.java` \u2014 top-level `@AutoConfiguration` entry point importing the above\n- `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactoryConfigurer.java` \u2014 bridges `KafkaProperties` into the factory\n\n**spring-framework** (core abstractions consumed by spring-kafka's containers):\n- `AsyncTaskExecutor.java`, `TaskExecutor.java`, `SimpleAsyncTaskExecutor.java` \u2014 the executor abstraction each child container/thread uses\n- `SmartLifecycle.java`, `Lifecycle.java` \u2014 the lifecycle contract `MessageListenerContainer` implements for phased start/stop ordering\n\nThis gives full visibility into the dependency chain (framework executor/lifecycle \u2192 kafka container/factory \u2192 boot autoconfiguration/properties) needed to plan the topological refactor order, concurrency-related breaking changes (e.g., `ContainerProperties.listenerTaskExecutor`, `ConcurrentMessageListenerContainer.setConcurrency`), and where spring-boot's `KafkaProperties.Listener.concurrency` maps through.",
